slots.the_counterexample_2026_08_20:
CONSTRUCTED, and it is why this row moved from `erased` to `compared`. `FuncTy` is `{ params, returns, is_vararg }`. A printed body shows its parameter types in the entry block header -- which the `param-type` lane already pins -- and shows its return types only through a `ret` an execution can reach. It shows `is_vararg` NOWHERE. So:

    rustcc fn @m::f(functy.7) {        rustcc fn @m::f(functy.8) {
    bb0(%0: ptr):                      bb0(%0: ptr):
        unreachable                        unreachable
    }                                  }

with `functy.7 = (ptr) -> bool` and `functy.8 = (ptr, ...) -> bool` are a NON-VARIADIC and a VARIADIC function. On AArch64 Apple and on x86-64 SysV those are different ABIs and calling one through the other's signature is undefined. Byte-identical but for one numeral, identical core module, identical interface -- and until 2026-08-20 `ir_mint::project` ACCEPTED BOTH. `functy_is_compared_and_the_vararg_pair_is_now_refused` builds the pair, asserts the core module still cannot separate it, and requires the gate to.
